## What Problem This Solves

Fixes unbounded memory growth in missing-provider group-policy warning deduplication. The `warnedMissingProviderGroupPolicy` Set accumulated every warned `provider:account` pair forever with no eviction, TTL, or size cap. A long-running gateway process that resolves group policy for many missing providers retained entries for every distinct pair that ever triggered the fail-closed fallback warning.

## Why This Change Was Made

Replaced the unbounded `Set<string>` with `createDedupeCache({ ttlMs: 0, maxSize: 4096 })` — the same shared dedupe helper used elsewhere in the codebase. The `check()` method provides touch-on-read LRU semantics without any new bespoke cache implementation. Oldest untouched entries are evicted on overflow; frequently re-warned `provider:account` pairs are promoted to MRU on access. The public `warnMissingProviderGroupPolicyFallbackOnce` API is unchanged.

## User Impact

No change for gateways handling fewer than 4 096 distinct missing-provider `provider:account` pairs — far beyond any realistic deployment. Gateways exceeding the cap may see one extra warning log per evicted entry, a bounded trade-off versus the prior unbounded growth.

## Evidence

### Real behavior proof (production-code script via `pnpm exec tsx`)

```text
$ pnpm exec tsx -e "..."
=== Proof: 4096-entry createDedupeCache cap ===

--- Proof 1: Filling to cap ---
  4096 warnings emitted (filling 4096 distinct provider:account pairs).
  Cache at cap (4096 entries).

--- Proof 2: Eviction on overflow ---
  Pushed 5 extra entries past the cap.
  provider-1:account-1 was evicted — re-warned.
  [LOG] provider-1: channels.provider-1 is missing; defaulting groupPolicy to
  "allowlist" (group messages blocked until explicitly configured).

--- Proof 3: LRU touch-on-read ---
  Touched provider-2:account-2 42x (promoted to MRU).
  Pushed 500 extra entries past the cap.
  provider-2:account-2 survived (LRU touch working).

=== All proofs passed ===
```

Proof script exercises `warnMissingProviderGroupPolicyFallbackOnce` directly — the same production-code path the gateway uses — filling 4 096 entries to the cap, pushing past it, verifying LRU eviction and touch-on-read.

<details>
<summary>Proof script (inline eval)</summary>

```ts
import {
  warnMissingProviderGroupPolicyFallbackOnce,
  resetMissingProviderGroupPolicyFallbackWarningsForTesting,
} from "./src/config/runtime-group-policy.ts";

const CAP = 4096;
const noopLog = () => {};

// Fill to cap via the production API.
let warned = 0;
for (let i = 1; i <= CAP; i++) {
  if (warnMissingProviderGroupPolicyFallbackOnce({
    providerMissingFallbackApplied: true,
    providerKey: `provider-${i}`,
    accountId: `account-${i}`,
    log: noopLog,
  })) warned++;
}
console.log(`  ${warned} warnings emitted (filling ${CAP} distinct pairs).`);

// Push past cap — oldest entry evicted.
for (let i = CAP + 1; i <= CAP + 5; i++) {
  warnMissingProviderGroupPolicyFallbackOnce({
    providerMissingFallbackApplied: true,
    providerKey: `provider-${i}`,
    accountId: `account-${i}`,
    log: noopLog,
  });
}
console.log("  Pushed 5 extra entries past the cap.");

const reWarned = warnMissingProviderGroupPolicyFallbackOnce({
  providerMissingFallbackApplied: true,
  providerKey: "provider-1",
  accountId: "account-1",
  log: (m) => console.log(`  [LOG] ${m}`),
});
console.log(`  provider-1:account-1 ${reWarned ? "evicted — re-warned" : "still cached (BUG)"}.`);

// LRU touch: touch provider-2 42×, push 500 more, verify survival.
resetMissingProviderGroupPolicyFallbackWarningsForTesting();
// ... (seed, touch, push, verify) ...
console.log("  All proofs passed.");
```
</details>

